NotoSansCJKsc-Bold-labels.otf

A subset of Noto Sans CJK SC Bold, version 2.004, from
https://github.com/notofonts/noto-cjk (Sans/OTF/SimplifiedChinese).
Copyright 2014-2021 Adobe (http://www.adobe.com/), with Reserved Font
Name 'Source'. Noto is a trademark of Google Inc. It is licensed under
the SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1, in OFL.txt beside this file.

It holds only the glyphs of the Simplified Chinese labels, the territory
sizes and the resource amounts (digits, "." "," "%", 万 and 亿), so it
stays a few kilobytes. Go Bold, from golang.org/x/image, draws every
other language. When a label needs a glyph this file lacks, a glyph
test in internal/territory or internal/web fails; make the subset again
with every glyph the labels need, with fontTools 4.55.3, from
Sans/OTF/SimplifiedChinese/NotoSansCJKsc-Bold.otf at the Sans2.004 tag
(sha256 b5f0d1a190a7f9b43c310a8850630af12553df32c4c050543f9059732d9b4c0a):

  python3 -m fontTools.subset NotoSansCJKsc-Bold.otf \
    --text=" 小中大型未知万亿0123456789.,%" --layout-features='' \
    --output-file=NotoSansCJKsc-Bold-labels.otf

The committed subset's sha256 is
8011926af635f6febbdf4d8da3d37224c5fbe2df434b30a535c0d63db2d62d14; a rebuild
differs from it only in the header's timestamps and checksums.
